# Named LogQL queries for `lq q <name> [args...]`.
#
# Format, one per line:   <name> [@datasource-uid] | <LogQL, $1..$9 as args>
#
# The optional @datasource binds a query to one Loki datasource. Without it a
# query runs against whatever `lq up` selected -- and against the wrong one it
# returns an empty result rather than an error, which reads as "nothing
# happened". Bind anything whose stream selector only exists in one place.
# Blank lines and #-comments are ignored. Arguments substitute literally --
# they are never passed through a shell.
#
# Copy this file to a *.logql there to activate it. Real packs live in ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/loki-queries/*.logql and are
# NOT tracked here: query templates encode a deployment's own namespaces, log
# schema and field names. Copy this file there and edit it.
#
# Cheap line filter FIRST, then `| json`, then the field match. `| json` parses
# every line it is given, so narrowing with |= "$1" beforehand is much faster
# over a wide window.

errors     | {namespace="$1"} | json | level="error"
by-field   | {namespace="$1"} |= "$2" | json | $3="$2"
grep       | {namespace="$1"} |= "$2"
